scripts/_tmp*

# gstack payload, materialized by `bash .claude/bootstrap-skills.sh`.
#
# The repo tracks exactly ONE thing per gstack skill: a RELATIVE `SKILL.md`
# symlink into `.claude/skills/gstack/`, which is itself ignored above.
# gstack 1.87 additionally materializes per-skill support trees (sections/,
# bin/, scripts/, src/, vendor/, references/, templates/, specialists/,
# migrations/) and whole new skill directories — 53 entries in this
# checkout, every one an ABSOLUTE symlink carrying this machine's own path.
# Committing one would break every other checkout, and would re-land the
# exact regression the 1.87.4 upgrade already caused once, when it rewrote
# the tracked SKILL.md symlinks from relative to absolute.
#
# They are regenerable from the command above, so they are ignored.
# Already-tracked files are unaffected: .gitignore never applies to a path
# git already tracks, so the existing SKILL.md symlinks stay tracked and
# their changes still show in `git status`. A genuinely new file that DOES
# belong in version control here needs `git add -f`.
.claude/skills/
